From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:07:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] renderer/d3d11: report the chosen driver to the debugger
 channel too

"Which rasterizer is this pane on" is a Phase 7 exit criterion (usable over
RDP, on WARP, with no fallback dialogs) and it had only ever been checked in
the standalone harness. A packaged Windows Terminal has no stdout and no
stderr, so the existing log.info line is invisible exactly where the question
matters.

Confirmed in a pane: driver=hardware feature_level=11_1.

zig build test passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/renderer/directx11/device.zig | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/renderer/directx11/device.zig b/src/renderer/directx11/device.zig
index 0e9213c70..ed7224b33 100644
--- a/src/renderer/directx11/device.zig
+++ b/src/renderer/directx11/device.zig
@@ -289,6 +289,13 @@ pub const Device = struct {
         log.info("D3D11 device ready: driver={t} feature_level={t} size={d}x{d}", .{
             chosen, level, width, height,
         });
+        // Also to the debugger channel: in a packaged Windows Terminal there is
+        // no stdout and no stderr, and "which rasterizer is this pane on" is a
+        // Phase 7 exit criterion that has only ever been checked in the
+        // standalone harness.
+        dbg("device: driver={t} feature_level={t} size={d}x{d}", .{
+            chosen, level, width, height,
+        });
         return self;
     }
 
